&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The greatest four-digit number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Concept Used:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The long&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;division method is used for finding the square root of the number&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; Greatest four-digit number = 9999&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Long division method for 9999&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/12/F1_Vinanti_Railway_09.12.22_D2.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 86px; height: 134px;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It gives the remainder 198&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For making the perfect square we have to subtract the number from the remainder&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Perfect Square = 9999 - 198= 9801&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hence, The Greatest Four Digit perfect square is 9801&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

