&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The correct answer is &amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;He requested me to open the door&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; &quot;&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;&quot; /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot; display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is an example of an&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;imperative sentence&lt;/span&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is in the form of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;direct speech&lt;/span&gt;. As per the question&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;we have to change it into indirect speech&lt;/span&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Basic rules for changing or converting&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;direct speech into indirect speech&lt;/span&gt;:​
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&amp;lsquo;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Comma&lt;/span&gt;&amp;rsquo; and &amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;inverted comma&lt;/span&gt;&amp;#39; are omitted in indirect speech and are often replaced by &amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&amp;#39; clauses to form &amp;#39;to clauses&amp;#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;According to the reporting verb, changes are made in the direct sentence or the sentence in inverted commas.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Said to&lt;/span&gt;&amp;#39; will be changed into &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;requested&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39; in the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;indirect speech&lt;/span&gt;. (reporting verb&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;can be changed to requested, ordered, suggested and advised, forbid-forbade, refused, promised, warned, agreed, commanded, proposed, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&amp;#39; conjunction will be added&amp;nbsp;to account for the comma and double-inverted commas (&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;starting a direct speech&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;An expression like please, kindly,&amp;nbsp;sir, madam, etc.&amp;nbsp;is omitted in Indirect speech.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This is the direct and indirect speech rule for the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;imperative sentence&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Example:&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;She said to her, &amp;quot;Please complete it&amp;quot;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;(direct speech)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;She requested her to complete it.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;(indirect speech)​&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;​&lt;/em&gt;Therefore, as per the points mentioned above, we find that&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;He requested me to open the door.&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the correct indirect form of the given sentence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to the question,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; a = &lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(3\over 4\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; (b + c)&amp;nbsp; or&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(4a\over3\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= b + c&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Substituting the value of &amp;quot;b + c&amp;quot; in the average equation,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(a+ {4a\over 3}\over3\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 63&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; a +&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(4a\over3\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 3&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 63&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(7a\over3\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 3&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 63&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp; a = &lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(3\times 3\times 63\over7\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;=&amp;nbsp;81&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; The value of a is 81.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

