&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Girls = 45%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Boys passed&amp;nbsp;= 75%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Girls passed&amp;nbsp;= 80%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Girls failed = 144&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Calculation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let total students = 400&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Girls = 45% = 45/100 &amp;times; 400 = 180&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Boys = 55% = 55/100&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 400 = 220&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Boys passed = 75%&amp;nbsp;= 3/4&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 220 = 165&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Boys failed = 220 - 165 = 55&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Girls passed = 80% = 4/5&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 180 = 144&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Girls failed = 180 - 144 = 36&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 36 units&amp;nbsp;= 144 (According to question)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 1 unit = 4&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Boys failed = 55&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 4 = 220&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; The correct answer is&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;220&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

