&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Price of an article is successively increased by 15% and 20%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then decreased by 10% and 5%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let the price article be 100.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 115/100&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 120/100&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 90/100&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 95/100 = 117990000/100000000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 11799/10000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Net Percentage Change = 11799 - 10000/10000&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 100 = 1799/100 = 17.99&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 18%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; The correct answer is 18% more.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

