		&lt;/tr&gt;
		&lt;tr&gt;
			&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:  (33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Implementing a strict attendance policy&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;focuses solely on punctuality but may not address the root cause of high turnover. It may be perceived as punitive and could contribute to dissatisfaction among employees.&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
		&lt;tr&gt;
			&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive salaries and benefits&lt;/strong&gt; are crucial factors in attracting and retaining talented employees. If the company is losing employees at a high rate, it may indicate that the current compensation package is not competitive in the market. Attracting and retaining skilled professionals is often closely tied to the overall compensation and benefits package. Offering competitive salaries, along with attractive benefits, can enhance the company&amp;#39;s ability to &lt;strong&gt;retain valuable talent&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
